          "question": "What does asthma guidance describe as the stepwise approach, and what changed about reliever choice?",
          "answer": "The guidance on asthma describes a stepwise approach to managing asthma, which typically involves adjusting treatment based on the severity and control of the condition. This approach starts with assessing the patient's symptoms and response to treatment. Depending on this assessment, healthcare providers may escalate or de-escalate therapy. The intent is to achieve the best control of asthma with the least amount of medication necessary.\n\nRegarding reliever choice, recent changes in guidelines have recommended that adults and adolescents with asthma use a low-dose inhaled corticosteroid combined with a short-acting beta-agonist (SABA) as needed for relief. This represents an update from previous recommendations where SABA was used alone for quick relief. \n\nI could not cover specific details about the stepwise levels or any personal recommendations for management. Always consult a healthcare provider for tailored advice.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
